            <!-- Philosophy -->
            <div class="philosophy-box">
                <h3><i class="fas fa-heart" style="color:var(--green,#4a7c00)"></i> Our Coaching Philosophy</h3>
                <p>
                    <strong>We believe soccer is a vehicle for growth.</strong> Every child who joins Sentinels
                    is met where they are and challenged to become better than they were yesterday. Our coaches
                    are here to nurture confidence, sharpen skill, and build the character that carries into
                    school, family, and every part of life after the whistle.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Development is not one-size-fits-all. A five-year-old learning to trap a ball, a twelve-year-old
                    fighting for a starting spot, and a high schooler chasing a college roster each need a different
                    kind of coaching â€” but all of them deserve the same care, patience, and belief. That is the
                    Sentinels standard, and every coach on our staff holds themselves to it.
                </p>
                <p style="margin-bottom:0">
                    We teach the technical foundations â€” dribbling, passing, shooting, defending, positioning.
                    We also teach the harder lessons: how to lose, how to lead, how to keep working when it is
                    not easy, and how to lift teammates up on the days they need it most. Those are the skills
                    that outlast any season.
                </p>
            </div>

